; combiner_even_mode.cnl — a symmetric two-way combiner, for brief-wsprobe-2 R-wsp2-14(f).
;
; Two identical transconductance devices drive a common load through equal arms. P0 splits the
; COMMON input node, so its series stimulus excites both halves in phase — which is what makes
; wsp_impedance(wsp, P0, P2) the EVEN-MODE load line at drain 2 rather than a one-port impedance
; (App. C, Eq. 196/197). By symmetry both branch currents are equal, the whole 2i flows in RL, and
;
;     V(d2)/iS(P2) = RM + 2*RL = 5 + 50 = 55 Ohm
;
; exactly — independent of gm, of RO and of frequency, which is the classic even-mode reduction and
; is what combiner_half.cnl reproduces with ONE branch and the load doubled.
;
; No ports (R-wsp1-6): the document's own fixtures have none either.
R:RSRC   s0 0    R=50 Ohm
WSProbe:P0  s0 ni

R:RIN    ni 0    R=1000 Ohm

VCCS:M1  d1 0  ni 0  G=0.05
R:RO1    d1 0    R=1000 Ohm
WSProbe:P1  d1 m1
R:RM1    m1 sum  R=5 Ohm

VCCS:M2  d2 0  ni 0  G=0.05
R:RO2    d2 0    R=1000 Ohm
WSProbe:P2  d2 m2
R:RM2    m2 sum  R=5 Ohm

R:RL     sum 0   R=25 Ohm

analysis SP1 type=sparam start=1 stop=3 npts=5 Unit=GHz
